        "id": "p2_t4_E_b660ff17",
        "question": "The cost of a notebook is twice the cost of a pen. Let the cost of the notebook be x and the pen be y. Which equation represents this statement?",
        "options": [
          "x - y = 2",
          "x - 2y = 0",
          "x + 2y = 0",
          "2x - y = 0"
        ],
        "answer": 1,
        "explanation": "The statement gives x = 2y, rewritten as x - 2y = 0 in the form ax + by + c = 0 as shown in Exercise 4.1 Q1.",
        "topic": 7,
        "level": "E",
        "prereq_id": 2,
        "category": "p2_t7_E",
        "category_label": "Word Prob · Level E",
        "source": "chapter_llm",
        "chapter_num": 4,
        "chapter_ref": "Ex 4.1 Q1"
      },
      {
